# --- Agent tooling ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A strategy installs nothing: the skills come with the researcher - see SETUP.md step 4.  Should
# somebody install them here anyway, everything APM downloads and writes is build output, ignored
# the way .venv/ is, so the AI setup stays per machine and the research tree stays research.
.agents/
.claude/
.codex/
.cursor/
.gemini/
.opencode/
.windsurf/
# The copilot target writes inside .github/ - only what APM puts there is ignored, so a workflow
# committed there later still shows up.
.github/skills/
.github/prompts/
.github/agents/
.github/instructions/
.github/copilot-instructions.md
apm_modules/
.mcp.json
apm.lock.yaml

# The per-machine fallback that loads a researcher when the assistant does not honour the loading
# variable - one line importing its CLAUDE.md by absolute path, so it never leaves this machine.
CLAUDE.local.md

# --- Step 1: Bibliotheca ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# The extracts a researcher's script pulls out of the PDFs - one file per chapter, so a book can be
# read a chapter at a time. They are the publisher's words under the publisher's copyright, and
# they come back with one command. The PDFs themselves are already ignored by the binary rule
# below; the notes ARE committed, because they are the reasoning.
Bibliotheca/Extracts/

# --- Step 2: Universe ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Regenerable from Investable_Universe.csv (which IS tracked - it is the seed the whole pipeline
# grows from) plus the data provider.
# Every table the universe notebook writes - the master, the register and any a strategy adds.
Universe/*.csv
!Universe/Investable_Universe.csv
Universe/Provider_Cache/

# --- Step 3: Data ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing under Data/ is committed except code. Every file here is either downloaded by
# Data/curator.py, derived by Data/refinery.py, or supplied by hand - see the template's README.
#
# The curator downloads the per-security time series, the benchmarks and the cash proxy. The index
# holdings and factor models attribution reads are dropped in by hand, because no price provider
# sells them.
Data/Curator/Time_Series/*.csv
Data/Curator/Time_Series/*.parquet
# Where a refresh resumes: each file's fetched-through date, and the provider's answer per name.
Data/Curator/*.json
# The provider's corporate actions a rebuilt adjustment reads, and the rebuild's file-by-file
# check against the provider's own adjusted prices: data, never committed.
Data/Curator/Actions/
Data/Curator/adjustment_checks.csv
# A copy of the curated files in the format a library reads, where it cannot read them as they
# are: rebuilt from the Parquet files, never committed.
Data/Curator/Engine/
Data/Curator/_history/
Data/Curator/Benchmarks/*.csv
Data/Curator/Benchmarks/*.parquet
Data/Curator/Benchmarks/*.xlsx
Data/Curator/Factors/*.csv
Data/Curator/Factors/*.parquet
Data/Refinery/Time_Series/*.csv
Data/Refinery/Time_Series/*.parquet

# Analyzer output: charts and the signal IC table, both rebuilt by Data/analyzer_marimo.py.
Data/Analyzer/Charts/
Data/Analyzer/*.csv

# --- Steps 4-6: Experiments ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every artefact an experiment produces is rebuilt by its notebook: the weight files, the
# summaries, the engine workbooks and the charts. None of it is committed. The `.gitkeep`
# negations are what keep the folder skeleton itself in the clone.
Experiments/*/Portfolio/*
Experiments/*/Backtest/*
Experiments/*/Attribution/*
!Experiments/*/Portfolio/.gitkeep
!Experiments/*/Backtest/.gitkeep
!Experiments/*/Attribution/.gitkeep

# --- Step 7: Paper trading --------------------------------------------------------------------
# A frozen book's code and FREEZE.json are committed: they are the book. What each day's run writes
# is not: the raw files linked into a book's folder, what its frozen refinery and engine write, the
# logs, and the record. The record is evidence that cannot be fetched again, so keep it in the
# database sink or back the folder up - see Paper_Trading/BITACORA.md. Nor is a book's frozen security master: it
# is the provider's data, as the one in Universe/ is, so it stays on the machine that froze the
# book, known by its hash in FREEZE.json - back it up with the record.
Paper_Trading/*/Universe/Security_Master.csv
Paper_Trading/*/Data/Curator/Time_Series/
# The index and factor files the daily run links in: licensed to a person, not to the repository.
Paper_Trading/*/Data/Curator/Benchmarks/
Paper_Trading/*/Data/Curator/Factors/
Paper_Trading/*/Data/Refinery/Time_Series/
Paper_Trading/*/Portfolio/
Paper_Trading/*/Backtest/
Paper_Trading/Logs/
Paper_Trading/Record/
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal

# --- Nothing binary, anywhere -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Charts, workbooks and papers are all either regenerated by the pipeline or licensed to a person
# rather than to the repository. Keeping them out is what keeps a clone small and its diffs
# readable. A marimo notebook never saves its outputs in its file, for the same reason.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.pdf
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.parquet
*.zip

# --- IDE --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- marimo ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# marimo keeps a session cache beside each notebook it runs: outputs, never committed.
__marimo__/

# --- File managers ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What Finder or Explorer leaves in a folder it shows: never part of the research.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Credentials -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The template is tracked; the filled-in file never is.
Config/.env
# A licence file the Lab's libraries read, if one is kept here.
.kaxanuk_license

# Python bytecode.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Local virtual environment. uv creates it on the first run; nothing in it is source.
.venv/
.ruff_cache/
